55,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I don't like Option A because of the fighting. Option B seems fair so everyone shares the spot!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I worry about Option C because of the time it takes, and Option A because of the summer smell. I prefer B.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option C requires too many man-hours and relies on people policing each other. Option B is the most logical compromise.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option B is the only one that's actually equal! No one gets stuck with the bins forever. I vote B!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option A is too costly for some budgets, and Option C creates social friction. Rotation teaches us to share the burden.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Kenji,,Everyone seems to like B! It's the friendliest way.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Shizue,,It is a gentle way to ensure no one feels singled out.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Provided the narrow frontages are managed, B is the most sustainable.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Rin,,Yes! Let's make it move!,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Servas,,"When we share the weight, the load becomes light for everyone.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
